<p>LLC « Medical Technologies of Dr. Renat Akhmerov» <a href="https://plasmolifting.online/">https://plasmolifting.online/</a></p>

<p>LLC « Medical Technologies of Dr. Renat Akhmerov» is a globally oriented medical company with full-cycle certified manufacturing of <strong><u>PRP tubes</u></strong>, Class III medical devices approved for IN VIVO use in all medical fields, including operating rooms, and holding official registration certificates.</p>

<p>The tubes comply with international quality standards ISO 13485 and GMP, which are mandatory for medical device</p>

<p>manufacturers in the European Union.</p>

<p> </p>

<p><strong>LLC «Medical Technologies of Dr. Renat Akhmerov» is currently looking for partners in Pakistan.</strong></p>

<p><strong>Interested members are requested to contact directly for further information:</strong></p>

<p>The Trade Representation of the Russian Federation in the Islamic Republic of Pakistan (Karachi Branch)</p>

<p>Торговое представительство Российской Федерации в Исламской Республике Пакистан (Отделение в г. Карачи)</p>

<p>Web: <a href="https://pak.minpromtorg.gov.ru/en/">https://pak.minpromtorg.gov.ru/en/</a></p>

<p>Facebook: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/The-Trade-Representation-of-Russia-in-Pakistan-104229818312715">https://www.facebook.com/The-Trade-Representation-of-Russia-in-Pakistan-104229818312715</a><br />
Phone: +92 21 3587-4393<br />
            +92 21 3587-4418</p>

<p> </p>

<p><strong><u>Invitation to Contribute to Pakistan Export Display Center at Embassy of Pakistan</u></strong></p>

<p>The Embassy of Pakistan, Doha is in the process of establishing a <strong>Pakistan Export Display Center</strong> within its premises as part of ongoing efforts to strengthen trade and commercial diplomacy and to project Pakistan’s export potential in a structured and dignified manner.</p>

<p>The Export Display Center is conceived as a permanent, <em>non commercial</em> exhibition space that will showcase Pakistan’s key export sectors through representative products, samples, and informational material. The display will highlight product categories, value chains, quality standards, and export strengths at a national level, without reference to individual companies, brands, or logos.</p>

<p>The focus will be on non-perishable export sectors such as rice (displayed in sealed acrylic boxes with labeled varieties), textiles, leather, sports goods, surgical instruments, handicrafts, marble, minerals, and other priority export categories.</p>

<p>Given your association’s role in representing and developing Pakistan’s export base, we invite your support and collaboration in:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Recommending representative product samples or sectoral display material</li>
	<li>Advising on appropriate sector narratives and product descriptions</li>
	<li>Participating in periodic rotation or thematic refresh of displays</li>
</ul>

<p>The Export Display Center will be viewed by a wide range of visitors, including government officials, foreign delegations, investors, buyers, diaspora members, and other stakeholders, and is expected to serve as a consistent source of interest and engagement within the Embassy.</p>

<p>Further details regarding display guidelines, contribution modalities, and rotation schedules will be shared in due course. Your expression of interest and preliminary inputs would be most appreciated.</p>

<p>We look forward to your cooperation in this initiative to collectively present Pakistan’s export strengths in an effective and coordinated manner.</p>

<p><strong>Interested members are requested to contact directly for further information:</strong></p>

<p><a>tia.doha@commerce.gov.pk</a></p>

<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>

<p><strong><u> Invitation to nominate exhibitors and potential buyers to participate in the 2nd National Fair — Spring 2026 (Vietnam)</u></strong></p>

<p>Vietnam will organize the 2nd National Fair — Spring 2026, one of four national fairs planned for 2026, aimed at promoting trade, technology transfer and business linkages between Vietnamese enterprises and international partners. The Fair targets sectors including textile and apparel, footwear, wood products, handicrafts and selected processing and manufacturing industries that supply Vietnam’s production and export chains.</p>

<p>To encourage participation and facilitate business matching, the Ministry of Industry and Trade has proposed the following support for foreign participants introduced by Vietnamese representative offices abroad:</p>

<p>Exhibiting enterprises: each foreign exhibitor introduced by a diplomatic or trade office will be offered one standard booth free of charge; free promotion and media exposure through the Fair’s general programs; complimentary participation in conferences, seminars and business‑matching events within the Fair; and free entry passes.</p>

<p>Potential buyers: each foreign buyer introduced by a diplomatic or trade office will be offered a free VIP entry pass and complimentary participation in conferences, seminars and business‑matching events within the Fair.</p>

<p>Detailed support mechanisms are being finalized and will be announced by the Ministry of Industry and Trade. Full event information and online registration are available at: <a href="http://vnf.vietrade.gov.vn/">http://vnf.vietrade.gov.vn</a> (<a href="http://vnf.vietrade.gov.vn/">vnf.vietrade.gov.vn</a> in Bing). The registration deadline is 17:00 (Hanoi time), 15 January 2026.</p>

<p>The Embassy respectfully requests the Chambers of Commerce and Industry in Pakistan to:</p>

<p>Publicize the Fair among Pakistani companies, especially those active in or supplying the textile‑garment, footwear, wood products, handicrafts and related manufacturing sectors.</p>

<p>Encourage and nominate qualified Pakistani enterprises to register as exhibitors or as potential buyers through the registration portal.</p>

<p>Facilitate contact between interested Pakistani companies and the Trade Promotion Agency of Vietnam for logistical and procedural support.</p>

<p>For event details and registration assistance, please refer to the Trade Promotion Agency (Ministry of Industry and Trade):</p>

<p>Address: 20 Ly Thuong Kiet, Cua Nam Ward, Hanoi, Vietnam</p>

<p>Contact: Mr. Hoang Tran Phuong — Phone: +84‑985431188; Email: <a>phuonghtr@moit.gov.vn</a>.</p>

<p>For coordination through the Embassy, please contact:</p>

<p>Economic and Trade Section, Embassy of Vietnam in Pakistan — Phone: 03333166868 (Mrs. Diep Ha - Head of Trade Officie in Karachi) or 03355656789 (Mr. Quang, Second Secretary) </p>

<p>The Embassy of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam avails itself of this opportunity to renew to the Chambers of Commerce and Industry the assurances of its highest consideration and looks forward to close cooperation to strengthen trade and business ties between Vietnam and Pakistan.</p>

<p>Yours faithfully,</p>

<p><strong>Vietnam Embassy in Pakistan</strong></p>

<p><strong>Tel: +92 51 2655785/87</strong></p>

<p><strong>Fax: +92 51 2655783</strong></p>

<p><strong>Website: <a href="https://vnembassy-islamabad.mofa.gov.vn/en-us/News/EmbassyNews/Pages/default.aspx">https://vnembassy-islamabad.mofa.gov.vn</a></strong></p>

